---
/*
  ============================================================
  LOZEN ADVISORY — DISCLOSURE-INDEPENDENCE LANDING PAGE
  src/pages/disclosure-independence-work-infrastructure/index.astro
  ============================================================

  OVERVIEW
  --------
  This is the primary conversion landing page for the
  disclosure-independence-work-infrastructure practice area.
  It is a fully self-contained Astro page — it does NOT use
  BaseLayout, the global Navigation component, or the global
  Footer. This is intentional: landing pages need independent
  header/footer control for conversion optimization.

  This file is the canonical template for future Lozen landing
  pages. When creating a new landing page, copy this file and
  update the data arrays in the frontmatter and the CSS tokens.

  ROUTE
  -----
  Resolves to: /disclosure-independence-work-infrastructure/
  File must remain at: src/pages/disclosure-independence-work-infrastructure/index.astro

  PAGE SECTIONS (in order)
  ------------------------
  1. Sticky Header        — wordmark, section nav, Request Briefing CTA
  2. Hero                 — dark navy, atmospheric blobs, Disclosure Risk Index panel
  3. Proof Strip          — 3 sourced statistics (Work Institute 2026, Catalyst 2026)
  4. Diagnostic Scorecard — 5-question quiz + Supabase submission + result modal
  5. Risk Frameworks      — left-list navigation + right content panel
  6. Reports & Research   — sculpted cards with icons + external/internal links
  7. Advisory Pre-Close   — full-width dark section with service specs + dual CTA
  8. Footer               — minimal, nav links, copyright

  ============================================================
  TYPOGRAPHY
  ============================================================

  This page uses a DIFFERENT font stack than the rest of the site.
  The site uses: Tenor Sans (display) + DM Sans (body)
  This page uses: Instrument Serif (display) + Work Sans (body)

  Both fonts are loaded via Google Fonts in the <head>:
    Instrument Serif: italic variant included (used in hero headline em)
    Work Sans: weights 400, 500, 600, 700

  The font tokens are overridden in the .lozen-landing token block:
    --font-display: "Instrument Serif", ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
    --font-sans:    "Work Sans", ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif;

  These overrides are scoped to .lozen-landing so they do not
  affect the rest of the site. Do NOT remove these overrides or
  the page will fall back to Tenor Sans/DM Sans.

  ============================================================
  COLOR SYSTEM
  ============================================================

  All colors are defined as CSS custom properties inside
  .lozen-landing to prevent bleed into other pages.

  NAVY FAMILY (dark surfaces: header, hero, scorecard, advisory, footer)
    --lz-navy-950: #0d2149  — hero background, header backdrop, footer
    --lz-navy-900: #162d5c  — section backgrounds
    --lz-navy-800: #1e3a6e  — secondary text, borders, icons on dark

  PAPER FAMILY (light surfaces: proof strip, quiz card, report cards)
    --lz-paper:   #ffffff   — primary white surface
    --lz-paper-2: #f5f7fa   — small UI elements only (answer index badge, modal chip)
    --lz-paper-3: #e4e9f0   — borders, dividers, progress dots (inactive)

  ACCENT YELLOW (CTA buttons, progress dots completed, risk panel bars)
    --lz-yellow-400: var(--color-accent-400, #f5e36b)
    --lz-yellow-500: var(--color-accent-500, #e7d35a)
    --lz-yellow-600: var(--color-accent-600, #b89c2d)
    Falls back to hardcoded values if global tokens are absent.

  TEAL ACCENT (Risk Frameworks section only)
    #3b6fa0 — eyebrow labels, rule under framework title, panel eyebrow
    This is pulled from the Lovable design system's --accent token.
    Not a CSS variable here — update manually if brand color changes.

  GREY WASH PREVENTION
  The site's global.css defines --color-base-50: #f7f9fc (blue-grey).
  This page overrides it:
    .lozen-landing-root { --color-base-50: #ffffff; background: #ffffff; }
  If grey wash returns, check this override is still present and that
  no section is using var(--color-base-50) without the override in scope.

  MODAL TIER COLORS (result modal top border + badge)
    Critical Alert:     border #c0392b, badge bg #fef3f2, text #c0392b
    Operational Drift:  border #d4880a, badge bg #fffbeb, text #92610a
    Strategic Resilience: border #27a060, badge bg #f0fdf4, text #166534
  Applied by JS via colorKey → CSS modifier class (--critical, --drift, --resilient)

  ============================================================
  QUIZ — ARCHITECTURE
  ============================================================

  The quiz is a multi-step diagnostic with 6 steps total:
    Step 0: Role selection (CFO / Board / CHRO / Other) — not scored
    Steps 1–5: Five diagnostic questions — scored 0, 0.5, or 1 each

  SCORING LOGIC
    Each question scores independently based on whether the answer
    reflects disclosure-independent architecture. The scoring direction
    varies per question because the questions are phrased differently:

    Q1 (Disclosure Independence) — "Yes" = bad (requires disclosure) → 0 pts
    Q2 (Invisible Attrition)     — "Yes" = good (detects before exit) → 1 pt
    Q3 (Power User Trap)         — "Yes" = bad (top performers unsupported) → 0 pts
    Q4 (Board Governance)        — "Yes" = good (succession accounts for non-disclosure) → 1 pt
    Q5 (Capital Efficiency)      — "Yes" = good (benefits = capital assets) → 1 pt

    In all cases: In Progress = 0.5 pts
    Total range: 0–5. Higher score = more resilient/disclosure-independent architecture.

    IMPORTANT: Do not assume "Yes always = bad" or "No always = good."
    Each question's score values are set explicitly in the quizQuestions array.
    Check the score property on each option before modifying questions.

  SCORING TIERS
    0–2:   Critical Alert       — reactive, absorbing full Invisible Attrition cost
    3–4:   Operational Drift    — right tools, wrong architecture
    5:     Strategic Resilience — disclosure-independent power user

  QUIZ DATA
  All question content is defined in the quizQuestions array in
  this frontmatter. To update a question, anchor stat, or answer
  option, edit that array only — do not touch the HTML template.

  QUIZ PROGRESS INDICATOR
  Six step dots rendered via [data-dot="N"] spans.
  Active dot: navy, scale 1.2
  Completed dot: yellow
  JS activates via .is-active / .is-complete classes in setStep()

  ============================================================
  SUPABASE INTEGRATION
  ============================================================

  Quiz submissions are posted from the browser on capture step
  completion. The result modal is NOT shown until the Supabase
  insert confirms success (response.ok === true). If the insert
  fails, the capture form re-enables and shows an inline error.
  This ensures every lead shown a result is recorded.

  ENDPOINT
    https://yaebacffmklidylcejlq.supabase.co/rest/v1/quiz_submissions

  CREDENTIALS (anon/public key — safe for browser use)
    apikey: sb_publishable_OiCvatOmGSEDBpx_9J2mew_AIeZyd3-
    RLS restricts to INSERT only. Do not replace with a service
    role key — that would expose full database access.

  SUPABASE POLICY CHANGE (May 30, 2026)
    New Supabase projects require explicit GRANTs in addition to RLS.
    These have been applied:
      grant usage on schema public to anon;
      grant insert on public.quiz_submissions to anon;
      grant usage on schema public to authenticated;
      grant select on public.quiz_submissions to authenticated;
    All existing projects are affected from October 30, 2026.

  TABLE SCHEMA (run supabase_quiz_setup.sql to create)
    id                    uuid (auto)
    created_at            timestamptz (auto)
    email                 text  — work email, required, validated client-side
    first_name            text  — optional
    role                  text  (cfo | board | chro | other)
    q1_disclosure         text  (yes | in_progress | no)
    q2_invisible_attrition text
    q3_power_user_trap    text
    q4_board_governance   text
    q5_capital_efficiency text
    score                 numeric(3,1)  (0.0–5.0)
    score_tier            text  (Critical Alert | Operational Drift | Strategic Resilience)
    referrer              text

  If table already exists, run to add new columns:
    alter table public.quiz_submissions
      add column if not exists email text,
      add column if not exists first_name text;

  ROW LEVEL SECURITY
    anon_insert_only: anon role can INSERT only
    auth_read: authenticated role can SELECT all

  PRIVACY
    email and first_name are PII. The page states: "Your information
    is used to deliver your scorecard result and to respond to your
    inquiry." Confirm this matches your privacy policy before launch.
    user_agent has been removed from the payload and schema — only
    referrer is retained for source attribution.

  To view submissions: Supabase Dashboard → Table Editor → quiz_submissions

  ============================================================
  REPORTS & RESEARCH CARDS
  ============================================================

  Cards are rendered from the `reports` array in frontmatter.
  Each card requires:
    eyebrow:  string — resource type label (all caps, small text)
    title:    string — resource name
    deck:     string — one-sentence description
    cta:      string — link label
    href:     string — URL (use trailing slash for internal routes)
    external: boolean — true opens in new tab with rel="noopener"
    iconType: string — key into cardIcons object (paper|layers|chart|tracker)

  To add a new card: add an entry to the reports array and
  add a corresponding SVG path string to the cardIcons object.
  Icons are 24×24 viewBox, stroke-based, currentColor.

  CARD SURFACE TREATMENT
  Cards use a 4-sided inset shadow stack to create physical depth:
    top:   white highlight (light source from top-left)
    bottom: navy shadow
    left:  white highlight
    right: navy shadow
  Plus 4 layered drop shadows at increasing radius/softness.
  The yellow top rule (4px) + 1px navy groove beneath it creates
  the "carved" brand mark. On hover: card lifts 4px, shadows deepen,
  yellow rule shifts from -400 to -500.

  ============================================================
  RISK FRAMEWORKS SECTION
  ============================================================

  Layout: CSS grid, 5fr (left list) / 7fr (right panel) at 800px+.
  Left column: section heading + deck + vertical nav rows.
  Right panel: ghost number (top-right, 8–14rem) + eyebrow + title
               + teal rule + body text. Min-height clamp(28rem, 45vw, 36rem).

  FRAMEWORK DATA
  Defined in the `tabs` array. Each entry:
    id:    string — used as tab-trigger/panel data attribute
    label: string — displayed in left nav row
    body:  string — panel body copy

  Panel eyebrow labels are hardcoded in the template JSX via
  conditional rendering on tab.id. If you rename a tab id, update
  the eyebrow conditionals in the framework panel template.

  TAB KEYBOARD BEHAVIOR
  Arrow keys navigate between rows (ARIA tablist pattern).
  Focus is managed via roving tabindex. The tab JS is in the
  data-tabs block — same logic as original tab system, unchanged.

  ============================================================
  HERO — DISCLOSURE RISK INDEX PANEL
  ============================================================

  The right-column panel in the hero is ILLUSTRATIVE DATA.
  The numbers (4.2%, 78%, 64%, 31%) are not client data.
  The "ILLUSTRATIVE" badge and disclaimer text make this explicit.

  The panel uses glassmorphism (rgba(255,255,255,0.05) + backdrop-filter: blur(16px))
  which requires a dark background behind it to be visible.
  If the hero background is changed to light, the panel will
  disappear. The panel is hidden below 960px (mobile/tablet).

  Progress bars in the panel are set via inline style="width:N%"
  directly in the HTML. To update the illustrative numbers,
  update both the data-val display span AND the inline width style.

  ============================================================
  PROOF STRIP — DATA SOURCES
  ============================================================

  The three statistics are sourced from published research.
  Do not change these numbers without updating the source attribution.
    74.69%  — Work Institute 2026 Retention Report, p.13
    42%     — Catalyst Inc., "Caregiving pressures top factor pushing
              women out of the workforce," January 29, 2026
    2×      — Work Institute 2026 Retention Report, p.6 (job security exits)

  ============================================================
  ADVISORY PRE-CLOSE SECTION
  ============================================================

  Sits between Reports & Research and the footer.
  Replaces the former "briefing rail" CTA card.
  Contains: headline, deck, primary CTA → /request-briefing/,
  secondary CTA → #reports (back-scroll), and three service
  spec chips (45 min, Pre-read, NDA).

  The secondary CTA "Or review the research first" links to
  the #reports anchor on the same page. This is intentional —
  it acknowledges the CFO/board audience often needs to review
  research before committing to a conversation.

  ============================================================
  ACCESSIBILITY
  ============================================================

  Role cards and answer options:
    - role="radio" + aria-checked + roving tabindex
    - Arrow keys (Up/Down/Left/Right) navigate within group
    - Home/End jump to first/last
    - Space/Enter select

  Tabs (Risk Frameworks):
    - role="tablist" / "tab" / "tabpanel"
    - Arrow keys navigate, Home/End jump
    - aria-selected managed on active tab

  Modal:
    - role="dialog" + aria-modal="true" + aria-labelledby="modal-title"
    - Focus trapped inside modal while open (trapFocus function)
    - Focus returns to trigger element on close
    - ESC key closes modal
    - Body scroll locked while open (document.body.style.overflow = "hidden")

  prefers-reduced-motion:
    All transitions and animations disabled via media query block
    at the bottom of the <style> block.

  ============================================================
  KNOWN CONSTRAINTS
  ============================================================

  1. Supabase anon key is in client-side code — this is by design.
     The key has INSERT-only RLS. Do not replace with a service
     role key, which would expose full database access.

  2. The file is ~2800 lines. This is intentional for a self-contained
     landing page. Do not extract sections into components unless
     you are building a reusable landing page system — premature
     componentization adds complexity without benefit here.

  3. The `<style is:global>` block is scoped manually via .lozen-landing
     prefix rather than using Astro scoped styles. This is required
     because the modal is a direct child of <body>, outside the
     component tree, and needs global CSS to be styled correctly.

  4. All internal hrefs must have trailing slashes. Astro + Vercel
     redirects non-trailing-slash URLs, which causes a redirect loop
     on the canonical URL. Always use /path/to/page/ not /path/to/page

  ============================================================
  MAINTENANCE CHECKLIST
  ============================================================

  When updating quiz questions:
    → Edit quizQuestions array in frontmatter only
    → Do not touch quiz HTML template

  When updating report cards:
    → Edit reports array in frontmatter
    → Add icon to cardIcons if new iconType needed

  When updating framework content:
    → Edit tabs array in frontmatter
    → If adding a tab, also add eyebrow label in the
      lozen-framework-panel__eyebrow conditional in the template

  When updating proof strip stats:
    → Update both the number and the source attribution text
    → Verify source is still accurate/accessible

  When updating Supabase table:
    → Update the submitToSupabase payload object in the <script> block
    → Run ALTER TABLE in Supabase SQL editor to add new columns
    → Update the RLS policies if read access needs to change
*/

